# Byte-exact test goldens and structure guards pin source text with \n-anchored
# regexes, so a CRLF checkout (Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true)
# fails seven tests on line endings alone. Force LF for every text file on
# checkout; binary detection stays automatic. Measured 2026-10-27 on PR #1037's
# windows-latest legs: the golden files diverged at line 1 ("golden: \r").
* text=auto eol=lf
